{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q426054","formula":"C₁₇H₂₂N₄O₂","hill":"C17H22N4O2","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":17.0,"H":22.0,"N":4.0,"O":2.0},"names":{"en":"Resiquimod"},"descriptions":{"en":"Resiquimod (R-848) is a drug that acts as an immune response modifier, and has antiviral and antitumour activity. It is used as a topical gel in the treatment of skin lesions such as those caused by the herpes simplex virus and cutaneous T cell lymphoma, and as an adjuvant to increase the effectiveness of vaccines. In an animal disease model, systemic administration of resiquimod-loaded nanoparticles has been shown to improve response rates to cancer immunotherapy with a checkpoint inhibitor through stimulation of tumor-associated macrophages."},"fame":7,"pubchemCid":159603,"mass":314.4,"charge":0,"smiles":"CCOCC1=NC2=C(N1CC(C)(C)O)C3=CC=CC=C3N=C2N","inchikey":"BXNMTOQRYBFHNZ-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"1-[4-amino-2-(ethoxymethyl)imidazo[4,5-c]quinolin-1-yl]-2-methylpropan-2-ol","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"159603","atoms":45,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":0.665,"y":2.771,"z":-1.131,"el":"O"},{"x":-3.826,"y":-0.889,"z":0.471,"el":"O"},{"x":-0.567,"y":0.416,"z":0.209,"el":"N"},{"x":-1.236,"y":-1.582,"z":-0.493,"el":"N"},{"x":2.388,"y":-2.342,"z":-0.359,"el":"N"},{"x":0.653,"y":-3.846,"z":-1.017,"el":"N"},{"x":-0.696,"y":1.793,"z":0.631,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.618,"y":2.835,"z":-0.505,"el":"C"},{"x":0.578,"y":-0.332,"z":0.091,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.623,"y":-0.374,"z":-0.15,"el":"C"},{"x":0.131,"y":-1.572,"z":-0.349,"el":"C"},{"x":1.939,"y":-0.06,"z":0.318,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.772,"y":4.242,"z":0.084,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.673,"y":2.617,"z":-1.591,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.017,"y":0.115,"z":-0.14,"el":"C"},{"x":2.815,"y":-1.136,"z":0.068,"el":"C"},{"x":1.067,"y":-2.578,"z":